{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"allpurpose-rainy-discus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# fsck snapshot rebuild silently drops history that exists only in a prior SNAPSHOT\n\n## Symptom\n214 tickets that were `closed` reverted to `in_progress` (194) or `open` (20) — 96 stories,\n53 tasks, 45 bugs, 20 epics. Status was not the only loss: 480 events total are missing from\ndisk (219 STATUS, 181 SIGNATURE, 64 COMMENT, 8 EDIT, 4 VERIFY_COMMANDS, 4 FILE_IMPACT).\nVerified zero legitimate reopens: no impacted ticket has a post-baseline STATUS event.\n\n## Root cause\nThree conditions compose:\n\n1. Compaction BEFORE `16640a705d` (2026-07-07, \"retire folded events to *.retired instead of\n   deleting\") DELETED folded source events. Their content survived only inside the SNAPSHOT's\n   `compiled_state`.\n2. `compact.rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` calls `reduce_ticket(ticket_dir,\n   include_retired=True)` (compact.py:474). Rebuild mode pre-strips SNAPSHOTs and replays raw\n   events from index 0 (`reducer/_replay.py:51-52`). That is correct ONLY IF the retired files\n   are a complete log — false for any ticket compacted before the Jul-7 fix.\n3. `rebar fsck --repair` (the A3 remediation, ticket 34b1) ran that rebuild at scale:\n   4 batches on 2026-08-05 22:13-22:41 PDT (+3 on 2026-07-08), touching 677 ticket dirs.\n\nFor each affected ticket the rebuild replayed only surviving files, so the newest surviving\nSTATUS (typically the `open -> in_progress` claim) became the reconstructed status.\n\n## Why the existing safety policy did not catch it\nTicket 34b1 already classifies STATUS/EDIT/FILE_IMPACT/SIGNATURE/VERIFY_COMMANDS as\nHUMAN-TRIAGE (\"order-sensitive ... surfaced, NOT auto-rebuilt\") vs AUTO-RECOVER\n(COMMENT/LINK/UNLINK/TAG_DELTA/COMMITS/BRIDGE_ALERT/REVERT). That classification gates only\nWHICH ORPHAN TYPE TRIGGERS a rebuild. A rebuild is whole-ticket: once triggered by an\nauto-recover orphan (or SNAPSHOT_STALE_CHANNEL), it rewrites ALL state from the incomplete\nlog, taking order-sensitive STATUS with it. The guard is on the trigger, not on the blast\nradius.\n\n## Secondary defect — `--dry-run` does not cover `--repair-snapshots`\n`fsck.py:582` passes `no_mutate` and ignores `dry_run`, so\n`rebar fsck --repair-snapshots --dry-run` MUTATES the store. Only the batched `--repair`\npath honors dry-run (fsck.py:541, 567). A read-only preview of the broad legacy rebuild is\ncurrently impossible.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` FAILS CLOSED for a ticket whose prior SNAPSHOT cites\n      `source_event_uuids` with no corresponding file on disk: refuse the rebuild, surface for\n      human triage, never write a lossy snapshot. Preserves the RC2b orphan-folding goal for\n      tickets whose log IS complete.\n- [ ] Rebuild seeds from the prior SNAPSHOT's `compiled_state` and replays only post-snapshot\n      events, so state that exists only in the snapshot is never discarded while the merged-in\n      orphan is still folded in.\n- [ ] `--dry-run` is honored on `--repair-snapshots` (and any other mutating fsck path):\n      prints the per-ticket plan, writes nothing. Regression test asserts no bytes change.\n- [ ] A store-wide fsck check reports every ticket whose SNAPSHOT cites missing source events\n      (the latent population), so exposure is visible before a repair runs.\n- [ ] Held-out tests: a ticket compacted in the legacy delete-style whose close exists only in\n      the snapshot must survive a rebuild attempt with status intact.\n\n## Remediation of existing damage (separate change)\nRestore the 480 deleted events from `origin/tickets` history (213/214 fully recoverable;\n`0241-c6c1-0a20-491b` is partial — one event has no deletion record), retire the bad\nAug-5/6 snapshots, then rebuild against the now-complete log. Note the `pre-a3-remediation`\ntag points at a MID-RUN commit (2026-08-05 22:33:05, after 2 of 4 batches), so it is NOT a\nsafe rollback point; the clean baseline is `bba514cd3318ea6b0e012e31656d3a088f419d1d`.","id":"b636-f31a-d590-4642","parent_id":"","priority":0,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"fsck snapshot rebuild silently drops history that exists only in a prior SNAPSHOT (214 tickets reverted from closed)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786255133635053001,"uuid":"0cac6af4-1b69-49b6-b0c2-0c3d4a451d05"}